# daddyshome bays
#
# One bay per line:  LABEL :: DIRECTORY :: PROMPT
#
# Leave PROMPT empty for a plain interactive session.
# Lines starting with # are ignored. Blank lines are ignored.
# Bays launch in order and tile across your screen, left to right, top to
# bottom. Four bays gives you a 2x2 grid.
#
# Copy this file to ~/.config/daddyshome/bays.conf and edit it.

PROJECT :: ~/code/my-project ::

REVIEW :: ~/code/my-project :: Read the last 10 commits and the current diff, then tell me what changed, what looks risky, and what still needs tests. Be concise and skip anything that looks fine.

INBOX :: ~/.local/share/daddyshome/inbox-brief :: Run `python3 fetch_inbox.py` and brief me on my email. Group what you find into: (1) needs a reply from me today, (2) anything time sensitive, (3) everything else worth knowing, (4) noise I can ignore. Quote only what is actually in the output. If the fetch fails, show me the error and stop.

STANDUP :: ~/code :: Give me a standup on my own work. For each git repo one level under this directory, check `git status --short` for uncommitted work and `git log --oneline -1` for the last commit. Then tell me: (1) what I touched in the last 3 days, (2) uncommitted work sitting around that might get lost, (3) branches with unpushed commits. Group by repo and skip repos with nothing going on.
